# Build context for docker/api.Dockerfile and docker/web.Dockerfile.
# Both only COPY backend/ and frontend/, but Docker still ships the whole
# context to the daemon — so size and secrets both matter here.

# Secrets. backend/core_api/.env holds the gateway key and deploy/local/.env
# holds AWS credentials; without these lines a COPY of backend/ would bake them
# into the image layers.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.env
**/.vault.key
**/data-vault/

# Dependencies and build output, rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/dist/
**/release/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Not needed to build either image. These unanchored patterns match the
# context root only, so the package READMEs the Python builds require
# (backend/*/README.md) are still included.
.git/
**/.github/
docs/
assets/
*.pdf
*.md
